"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Notehead-swift.struct/!=(_:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"!="},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/notehead-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Notehead-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)","title":"!=(_:_:)"}}}